The local control socket can apply a value to the running process only, but
every path it sets is marked dirty, so the next persist from any caller writes
those values into the user layer. Transient runtime changes -- a privacy
throttle, a mic mute -- silently became saved configuration.

A blanket runtime-only socket is not an option: the web UI stages page edits
over the same socket and relies on an explicit save_config to commit them.
Make the runtime behaviour opt-in instead. imp-control and microphone send
RUNTIME, and only that transport keeps its paths out of the dirty set. The
flag is per thread because every IPC client runs in its own thread, so one
client cannot silence another's staging.

